    "coverImage": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Mahabodhitemple.jpg/1280px-Mahabodhitemple.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail",
    "description": "The supreme sanctuary of global Buddhism where the Mahabodhi Temple and the sacred Bodhi Tree mark the exact spot where enlightenment dawned upon humanity.",
    "longDescription": "Under the spreading branches of the sacred Peepal tree, Prince Siddhartha sat on the Vajrasana (Diamond Throne) and vowed not to move until he unlocked the truth of existence. The demon of illusion, Mara, unleashed armies of monsters, temptresses, and raging storms. Siddhartha calmly touched the ground with his right hand in the Bhumisparsha Mudra, calling the Earth Mother to bear witness to his lifetimes of virtue. The earth quaked, Mara’s illusions shattered, and the morning star rose on the awakened Buddha.\n\nEmperor Ashoka visited Bodh Gaya around 260 BCE and constructed the original diamond shrine. The present 55-meter grand pyramidal temple dates back to the Gupta Empire (5th–6th century CE), surrounded by ancient stone railings carved with lotus medallions, centaurs, and winged beasts.\n\nBodh Gaya invites wanderers to step into living chapters of sacred lore and timeless folklore in Bihar.",
    "loreTitle": "The Diamond Throne & The Earth-Touching Miracle",
    "ancientLegend": "Under the spreading branches of the sacred Peepal tree, Prince Siddhartha sat on the Vajrasana (Diamond Throne) and vowed not to move until he unlocked the truth of existence. The demon of illusion, Mara, unleashed armies of monsters, temptresses, and raging storms. Siddhartha calmly touched the ground with his right hand in the Bhumisparsha Mudra, calling the Earth Mother to bear witness to his lifetimes of virtue. The earth quaked, Mara’s illusions shattered, and the morning star rose on the awakened Buddha.",
    "historicalChronicle": "Emperor Ashoka visited Bodh Gaya around 260 BCE and constructed the original diamond shrine. The present 55-meter grand pyramidal temple dates back to the Gupta Empire (5th–6th century CE), surrounded by ancient stone railings carved with lotus medallions, centaurs, and winged beasts.",
    "folkloreTales": [
      "The Immortal Bodhi Sapling: When King Ashoka sent his daughter Sanghamitta with a branch of this original tree to Sri Lanka, that sapling thrived at Anuradhapura. Cuttings from it were later brought back to Bodh Gaya to replant the tree after invaders cut it down, preserving an unbroken genetic line for 2,500 years.",
      "The Lotus Footprint Walk (Chankramana): Along the northern side of the temple lies a raised stone platform adorned with 19 carved lotuses, commemorating the spots where lotus flowers miraculously sprang from the earth under the Buddha’s footsteps."
    ],
