    "coverImage": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Golghar_%E0%A5%AA.jpg/1280px-Golghar_%E0%A5%AA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail",
    "description": "Rising along the southern bank of the Ganges, Patna is ancient Pataliputra—the imperial capital of Emperor Ashoka and Chandragupta Maurya, and the holy birthplace of Guru Gobind Singh.",
    "longDescription": "According to myth, King Putraka created Pataliputra with magical powers for his queen Patali. Greek ambassador Megasthenes marveled at the city with 64 gates and 570 towers surrounded by deep moats filled with Ganges water. It was the nerve center from which Chanakya penned the Arthashastra and unified India.\n\nExcavations at Kumhrar revealed the monumental 80-pillared Mauryan assembly hall. In 1666, the tenth Sikh Guru, Guru Gobind Singh, was born here; the white marble Takht Sri Patna Sahib stands as one of the five supreme seats of Sikh spiritual authority.\n\nPatna invites wanderers to step into living chapters of sacred lore and timeless folklore in Bihar.",
    "loreTitle": "The Golden City of the Mauryas & The Takht of the Tenth Master",
    "ancientLegend": "According to myth, King Putraka created Pataliputra with magical powers for his queen Patali. Greek ambassador Megasthenes marveled at the city with 64 gates and 570 towers surrounded by deep moats filled with Ganges water. It was the nerve center from which Chanakya penned the Arthashastra and unified India.",
    "historicalChronicle": "Excavations at Kumhrar revealed the monumental 80-pillared Mauryan assembly hall. In 1666, the tenth Sikh Guru, Guru Gobind Singh, was born here; the white marble Takht Sri Patna Sahib stands as one of the five supreme seats of Sikh spiritual authority.",
    "folkloreTales": [
      "The Agam Kuan Chamber of Ashoka: The unfathomable deep brick well of Agam Kuan is rumored to have been Emperor Ashoka’s fiery torture chamber before his transformation at Kalinga.",
      "The Flying Arrows of Takht Sahib: Sacred relics preserved at Patna Sahib include golden arrows and miniature armors blessed by the warrior-saint Guru Gobind Singh during his childhood."
    ],
