    "description": "Fringed by golden palms and azure Arabian waters, North Goa is a vibrant tapestry of 17th-century Portuguese battlements, flea markets, and coastal bohemian folklore.",
    "longDescription": "Hindu mythology says Goa (Gomantak) was brought forth from the sea when Lord Parashurama shot his flaming arrow into the Arabian Sea from the Sahyadri mountains, commanding the ocean waters to retreat and uncover a fertile paradise for sages and scholars.\n\nIn 1612, the Portuguese constructed the massive Fort Aguada with 79 cannons and a colossal freshwater spring (Aguada means water) where merchant galleons sailing across the Cape of Good Hope refilled their freshwater barrels. Later in the 1960s, the psychedelic Anjuna flea market transformed North Goa into the global capital of free spirits and electronic dance music.\n\nNorth Goa invites wanderers to step into living chapters of sacred lore and timeless folklore in Goa.",
    "loreTitle": "The Aguada Fort Waters & The Hippie Trail of Anjuna",
    "ancientLegend": "Hindu mythology says Goa (Gomantak) was brought forth from the sea when Lord Parashurama shot his flaming arrow into the Arabian Sea from the Sahyadri mountains, commanding the ocean waters to retreat and uncover a fertile paradise for sages and scholars.",
