    "coverImage": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Igreja_Paroquial_de_Santiago_de_Amorim.JPG/1280px-Igreja_Paroquial_de_Santiago_de_Amorim.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail",
    "description": "The sun-drenched riverside capital of Goa, famous for its labyrinthine Portuguese Latin Quarter of Fontainhas, azulejo hand-painted ceramic tiles, and vibrant riverfront promenades.",
    "longDescription": "The name Panaji derives from \"Panjanahani\", meaning \"the land that never floods.\" Local legend tells of the Phoenix fountain (Fonte Phoenix), a freshwater spring tucked into the hillside that sustained the city’s founders during long monsoons and was believed to be blessed with everlasting purity.\n\nPanaji succeeded Old Goa as the seat of the Viceroy in 1843. The iconic Church of Our Lady of the Immaculate Conception, with its gleaming white baroque zigzag staircase built in 1619, served as the first landmark seen by Portuguese sailors arriving from Lisbon across the open sea.\n\nPanaji invites wanderers to step into living chapters of sacred lore and timeless folklore in Goa.",
    "loreTitle": "The Latin Quarter of Fontainhas & The Sunset on the Mandovi",
    "ancientLegend": "The name Panaji derives from \"Panjanahani\", meaning \"the land that never floods.\" Local legend tells of the Phoenix fountain (Fonte Phoenix), a freshwater spring tucked into the hillside that sustained the city’s founders during long monsoons and was believed to be blessed with everlasting purity.",
    "historicalChronicle": "Panaji succeeded Old Goa as the seat of the Viceroy in 1843. The iconic Church of Our Lady of the Immaculate Conception, with its gleaming white baroque zigzag staircase built in 1619, served as the first landmark seen by Portuguese sailors arriving from Lisbon across the open sea.",
    "folkloreTales": [
      "The Red Tiles of Fontainhas: Portuguese colonial law required homeowners to repaint their facades every year after the monsoon using vibrant yellow, indigo, and terracotta natural lime pigments, giving the quarter its timeless Mediterranean glow.",
      "The Ghost of the Adil Shahi Palace: The oldest surviving building in Panaji, the 1500 CE summer palace of Sultan Adil Shah of Bijapur, is said to echo with the distant sound of Persian sitars in its deepest arched cellars."
    ],
