    "coverImage": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/1000_Year_loop.jpg/1280px-1000_Year_loop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail",
    "description": "Known as \"The Middle Land\" between India and Tibet, Spiti is an otherworldly high-altitude desert of barren moonscapes, ancient fortress monasteries, and 500-million-year-old ocean fossils.",
    "longDescription": "According to Tibetan lore, Spiti’s sheer canyon cliffs were the battleground where Guru Padmasambhava (Guru Rinpoche) subdued fierce mountain demons with his dorje thunderbolt, converting them into protectors of the Dharma. Tabo Monastery, founded in 996 CE, is celebrated as the \"Ajanta of the Himalayas\" for its pristine 1,000-year-old frescoes and stucco statues.\n\nPerched precariously at 13,668 feet atop a conical hill overlooking the Spiti River, Key Gompa resembles a multi-storied castle fortress, having survived multiple Mongol and Dogra sieges across a millennium. The high village of Langza is famous for marine ammonite fossils (Shaligrams) from the ancient Tethys Sea that existed before the Himalayas rose.\n\nSpiti invites wanderers to step into living chapters of sacred lore and timeless folklore in Himachal Pradesh.",
    "loreTitle": "The Fortress Monastery of Key & The Mummified Monk of Giu",
    "ancientLegend": "According to Tibetan lore, Spiti’s sheer canyon cliffs were the battleground where Guru Padmasambhava (Guru Rinpoche) subdued fierce mountain demons with his dorje thunderbolt, converting them into protectors of the Dharma. Tabo Monastery, founded in 996 CE, is celebrated as the \"Ajanta of the Himalayas\" for its pristine 1,000-year-old frescoes and stucco statues.",
    "historicalChronicle": "Perched precariously at 13,668 feet atop a conical hill overlooking the Spiti River, Key Gompa resembles a multi-storied castle fortress, having survived multiple Mongol and Dogra sieges across a millennium. The high village of Langza is famous for marine ammonite fossils (Shaligrams) from the ancient Tethys Sea that existed before the Himalayas rose.",
    "folkloreTales": [
      "The 550-Year-Old Mummy of Sangha Tenzin: In the remote hamlet of Giu sits the naturally preserved, cross-legged mummy of a Buddhist monk discovered after an earthquake in 1975, with hair, skin, and teeth completely intact without any chemical embalming.",
      "The World’s Highest Post Office: At Hikkim (14,567 ft), travelers send handwritten postcards stamped from the world’s highest postal station, carried down mountain gorges on foot by resilient postal runners."
    ],
